summary:
Fidelity and consistency review of /home/zhengyew/telelean/verbatim_prompt_log/bundle_21/user_requested_documents/01_spec_v4.md, checked against prompt21.md, all three mid-turn messages in prompt21_midturn.md, v3.1 and the code. The review was read-only.

Every turn-21 paragraph (¶1–¶12) and every ★D1–★D6 answer is captured by some clause, and Part 4 explains most departures. I found no blockers. There are 11 major findings, 17 minor and 1 nit.

1. **The user's third mid-turn message is missing from v4.** It was queued at 15:36:19Z (23:36 local), two minutes after v4 was saved (23:34:14). It asks for two things:
   - a fixed, unchanging session base, with the Current tab completely uneditable. v4's ES-7 (hand edits merged into the base) and its knock-on clauses do the opposite (F1);
   - undo/redo whose Current and Proposed histories never interact. v4 never mentions Redo and puts everything on one Undo (F2).

2. **The new arrow and glow model contradicts unchanged or partly updated clauses:**
   - RV-6 leaks proof results through the now-transitive green glow (F5);
   - the band and the §13.7 guarantee overclaim when a proof uses a card that has no arrow; TL107's coverage exemption is never removed (F7, F8);
   - CF-7 makes proof-used (solid) arrows impossible to freeze, contradicting FZ-13 (F3);
   - a target selected through its "follows from nothing" mark can receive Claude's arrows, but only the user may remove the mark (F4);
   - with the whole model open, proofs of non-target cards have no question and no permitted set (F6).

3. **Two autopilot items don't work as written:**
   - AR-8's ★D7 dialog fails for an unformalised source and inside a session (F9);
   - Part 4's "unless you unfreeze arrows" is false under ES-2's preset (F10).

4. **The autopilot log is incomplete.** It claims to list every choice made without asking, yet it omits the clause-level departures from the user's own words (F11).

**Minor and nit findings:**
- stale wording from v3.1's ★D1(a), in TR-13's "Delete anyway" (F12);
- departures that are untagged or wrongly tagged: AR-6, AR-2, the whole-model switch (F13, F14);
- gesture conflicts in CM-7 (F15), and the FZ-4 and FZ-9 lists not updated for arrows (F16);
- terminology clashes (F25–F28):
  - dotted vs dashed;
  - "✓ proved" used for established cards;
  - "pending item" used for items in review;
  - RV-5's "Dependencies" title clashing with the new Dependencies field;
  - axiom card vs Lean axiom;
- edge cases a builder would hit: verdict overlap (F17), Claude-added intermediate cards (F19), old ASSUMPTION blocks with premises (F20), unselected arrows (F23), and arrow drawing in the Proposed view (F24).

