findings.problem:
§13.7 says, without conditions, that every card a proof uses has an arrow into the proved card. A16 and A20 describe states where this is false. BD-5 says only hand-written proofs can produce such arrows, but A16 is a deletion, not a hand-written proof.
Nothing stops Claude creating such a state either:
- with the whole model open, B.3 lets it remove any unselected, unfrozen arrow, including one a non-target's proof uses;
- B.2 checks targets only;
- RV-7 says removing an arrow is never an own-Accept item, so a group Accept can apply it.

The user asked that every design decision taken for them on autopilot be logged so they can reverse it. Part 2 and the log list only ★D7 and ★D8, and the log claims to list every choice made without asking.
But v4 also departs, without asking, from the user's own turn-21 words:
- green means established, not proved (BD-6);
- Claude only adds arrows under the preset (ES-2);
- any card, or the 'follows from nothing' mark, moves an axiom to the canvas (AR-6);
- Move to axioms drops the proof (AR-7);
- the right-click menu replaces VS Code's (CM-7);
- DO-0 defines what 'the relevant cards' are;
- the whole-model switch keeps standing freezes.
Part 4 gives reasons for these but no way to reverse them, so the log's claim to completeness is false.

CM-7 selects the right-clicked thing first unless it is already selected, which replaces the selection. This breaks two gestures:
- AR-1's 'select one or more cards, right-click the target, and choose Draw arrows from the selection' loses its sources;
- the empty-canvas menu's 'Tidy layout' ('re-places the selected cards') has nothing left selected after the right click.

The AXIOMS header claims the column accounts for every belief, but two kinds of assumption are not counted:
- pending propositions, which are Lean axioms on the canvas and which v4 itself treats as assumptions (S16);
- definitions, which can carry beliefs (S5).

v4 gives existing words new meanings without renaming their old uses:
- 'pending', now a proof state, is still used for items in review ('pending item(s)');
- 'Dependencies', now a card field, is still RV-5's title for item-to-item dependencies, which makes 'dependencies' in ES-7 and RV-11 ambiguous;
- 'claimed', renamed to 'pending' for proofs, is reused for arrows.

Now that 'axiom' is a card kind, several clauses use 'axiom(s)' ambiguously:
- Terms' 'resting only on axioms', where BD-6 also allows presuppositions and definitions;
- Backstop (a)'s 'every axiom', which means Lean axioms;
- B.5's 'every card in its footprint is an axiom card', while Terms count presuppositions as (vocabulary) cards.
BD-6 also says both 'hidden axiom' and 'hidden assumption' for the same thing (TL103).
